{
  "slug": "hunter-for-claude",
  "name": "Hunter For Claude",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Find and organize companies without leaving Claude. This app connects directly to Hunter to help you discover businesses that match your criteria, enrich them with reliable company-level data, and save the ones you care about.\n\nYou can search for companies using natural language (for example, by location, industry, size, or technologies), review results with domain-level insights, and enrich any company to get structured information such as industry, headcount range, headquarters location, and tech stack. When a company looks relevant, you can save it straight to your Hunter Leads for later use.\n\nDesigned for sales, marketing, and research workflows, the app focuses on fast exploration and clean company data. No personal data, no guesswork, just actionable company insights inside Claude.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **13 skills** and **1 MCP server**.\n\n- **Skills** (13): `build-sequences` (Builds and runs email outreach sequences end to end — create a sequence, add follow-up steps and message…), `check-usage` (Reports the Hunter account's plan, remaining credits, and usage), `company-enrichment` (Retrieves detailed company information including industry, size, location, and description from a domain name), `company-lists` (Saves companies and organizes them into Hunter company lists — save a company, add/remove companies to lists, create…), `discover` (Finds companies matching criteria (industry, size, location, technologies), estimates how many contacts exist across them, and manages saved…), `domain-search` (Finds all publicly available email addresses and contacts at a company domain), `email-finder` (Finds a professional email address from a person's name and company domain), `email-verifier` (Verifies whether an email address is deliverable by checking DNS and SMTP records), and 5 more\n- **MCP servers** (1): `hunter`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install hunter-for-claude@claude-community` from `hunter-io/claude-plugin`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude",
    "copilot",
    "codex"
  ],
